WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.001 --> 00:01.095
(All characters, locations, and events are fictional

3
00:01.120 --> 00:02.182
and for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:02.207 --> 00:03.253
No actions depicted are intended to be encouraged or endorsed.

5
00:03.278 --> 00:04.333
Animals were specially trained and supervised by professionals.

6
00:04.357 --> 00:05.452
Viewer discretion is advised.)

7
00:06.994 --> 00:09.458
They say golf is a game of focus.

8
00:11.085 --> 00:12.797
But to me, it's a game

9
00:12.822 --> 00:15.202
that teaches us how to stay with someone long enough.

10
00:15.358 --> 00:18.103
Eighteen holes are long enough to see someone smile,

11
00:18.128 --> 00:20.128
long enough to see them frustrated,

12
00:20.282 --> 00:23.673
and long enough to know if you still want to walk beside them.

13
00:23.698 --> 00:25.643
On the course, we may each play our own shot,

14
00:25.668 --> 00:27.896
see things differently, and stumble on different holes.

15
00:27.921 --> 00:30.704
But in the end, we're still heading the same way.

16
00:31.061 --> 00:32.355
Love is no different.

17
00:32.380 --> 00:34.525
It's not about hitting the perfect shot every time.

18
00:34.550 --> 00:36.318
It's about not leaving each other behind,

19
00:36.343 --> 00:37.896
even when the ball lands in a bunker.

20
00:37.921 --> 00:39.919
Maybe what makes this game special

21
00:39.944 --> 00:42.022
isn't the birdies or the eagles,

22
00:42.047 --> 00:44.535
but hearing someone quietly say,

23
00:44.560 --> 00:47.027
"It's okay. We'll try again. We'll keep going together."

24
00:47.729 --> 00:49.842
Because in golf, you may have to swing alone.

25
00:49.867 --> 00:52.652
But in love, you should never have to walk alone.

26
00:53.091 --> 00:56.491
And if you find someone who'll play every season by your side,

27
00:56.516 --> 00:58.008
no matter how long the fairway,

28
00:58.033 --> 00:59.357
your heart will never grow tired.

29
01:01.377 --> 01:04.552
(Pro Meiji - Jenjira Jinangkul)

30
01:10.824 --> 01:14.308
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

31
01:15.008 --> 01:16.669
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

32
01:16.694 --> 01:20.219
♪ It's plain to see ♪

33
01:20.737 --> 01:22.477
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

34
01:22.502 --> 01:25.900
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

35
01:26.554 --> 01:28.371
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

36
01:28.396 --> 01:31.858
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

37
01:32.275 --> 01:34.140
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

38
01:34.165 --> 01:37.000
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

39
01:37.025 --> 01:38.939
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

40
01:38.964 --> 01:41.726
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

41
01:41.751 --> 01:44.643
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

42
01:44.668 --> 01:48.448
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

43
01:48.473 --> 01:50.315
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

44
01:50.340 --> 01:53.230
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

45
01:53.255 --> 01:56.813
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

46
01:56.838 --> 02:01.550
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

47
02:01.575 --> 02:03.575
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

48
02:05.013 --> 02:07.898
I'm thinking of getting a new manager.

49
02:07.923 --> 02:09.497
You can't do this to me, Nana.

50
02:09.895 --> 02:11.710
Besides, we're family.

51
02:11.735 --> 02:14.269
Family shouldn't steal from family.

52
02:14.371 --> 02:15.731
Nut.

53
02:15.756 --> 02:19.176
I have six months to make this place profitable again.

54
02:19.201 --> 02:22.905
So I need someone experienced and trustworthy to help me.

55
02:22.930 --> 02:24.104
Wait. Me?

56
02:24.155 --> 02:25.806
Dark chocolate. It's a little bitter.

57
02:25.831 --> 02:27.520
It might taste bitter at first,

58
02:27.545 --> 02:29.905
but I think there's a little sweetness underneath.

59
02:29.930 --> 02:32.495
Kind of like someone I know. Acts all tough,

60
02:32.520 --> 02:33.979
but she's secretly sweet.

61
02:38.247 --> 02:40.795
Do you know why I gave you two weeks

62
02:40.820 --> 02:42.820
to conquer the hardest hole?

63
02:43.901 --> 02:45.689
To put pressure on me?

64
02:45.990 --> 02:47.261
No.

65
02:47.657 --> 02:51.275
I wanted to see how long you'd stick with it.

66
02:51.300 --> 02:53.237
Because if you're only doing this to beat me,

67
02:53.370 --> 02:54.915
you might give up halfway.

68
02:56.601 --> 02:59.553
But if you're doing it to overcome your own limits,

69
03:01.842 --> 03:03.831
then this hole won't just be a condition.

70
03:05.322 --> 03:07.322
It'll prove that

71
03:08.061 --> 03:09.795
no matter what comes your way,

72
03:10.677 --> 03:12.383
you won't give up easily.

73
03:13.229 --> 03:14.809
And you won't run from it.

74
03:15.373 --> 03:17.690
You'll be ready to give it everything you've got.

75
03:18.746 --> 03:20.076
And if you pull it off,

76
03:20.322 --> 03:22.195
I'll give you my full support.

77
03:33.862 --> 03:37.220
Thank you, everyone, for coming to support me.

78
03:37.754 --> 03:38.794
You got this!

79
03:38.999 --> 03:41.266
Give it your all, Miss Nana!

80
03:41.543 --> 03:43.400
What I'm about to do

81
03:43.425 --> 03:46.135
isn't just about meeting Pro Vee's challenge.

82
03:48.277 --> 03:50.609
If I'm going to run this course,

83
03:51.045 --> 03:53.823
I want to start by showing everyone

84
03:54.003 --> 03:58.067
that I'm serious and ready to face whatever comes my way.

85
03:58.614 --> 04:02.167
It means so much to have everyone behind me.

86
04:14.761 --> 04:16.596
No matter how it turns out,

87
04:16.889 --> 04:18.889
I want everyone to know

88
04:20.394 --> 04:22.203
that I really gave it my all.

89
04:30.926 --> 04:33.789
Wow! Great shot!

90
04:33.948 --> 04:36.559
That was beautiful, Miss Nana!

91
04:48.349 --> 04:49.694
Beautiful.

92
05:00.366 --> 05:02.453
I called this urgent meeting today

93
05:02.660 --> 05:04.215
because I have an announcement.

94
05:06.269 --> 05:07.961
Starting today,

95
05:09.127 --> 05:13.398
March will be taking over as manager

96
05:13.423 --> 05:15.121
of the Royal Green Golf Club.

97
05:21.282 --> 05:24.785
As for Mr. Thiti, who's held the position for years

98
05:24.810 --> 05:26.303
with nothing to show for it,

99
05:26.790 --> 05:29.743
I've transferred him to manage my hotel in Chiang Rai.

100
05:40.243 --> 05:43.267
Why does everyone look so surprised?

101
05:43.775 --> 05:45.227
A round of applause, please.

102
05:52.958 --> 05:54.481
Surely you can do better than that.

103
05:55.033 --> 05:58.041
Let's show some Royal Green spirit.

104
06:21.102 --> 06:22.794
Nice ball position.

105
06:25.495 --> 06:28.960
Nana's really something.

106
06:29.183 --> 06:31.723
It's not often we get to see the little one's fighting spirit.

107
06:31.748 --> 06:33.033
She takes after her father.

108
06:33.686 --> 06:35.927
I mean her determination and drive.

109
06:35.952 --> 06:37.952
Just look at her eyes, sir.

110
06:38.588 --> 06:39.731
Oh, thanks.

111
06:39.852 --> 06:42.218
Beginner's luck, maybe?

112
06:42.282 --> 06:44.022
One shot and you're all impressed already?

113
06:44.047 --> 06:45.626
Hole 7 isn't easy, you know.

114
06:47.017 --> 06:49.585
Come on, August. Show her some support.

115
06:50.284 --> 06:52.167
If you can do this, Nana,

116
06:52.421 --> 06:54.731
I'll do my part to help you turn this course around.

117
06:59.766 --> 07:01.603
Give it your all, Miss Nana!

118
07:16.318 --> 07:17.986
Oh! Into the water!

119
07:19.266 --> 07:20.281
Whoa.

120
07:31.123 --> 07:33.582
There's a one-stroke penalty for hitting it into the water.

121
07:33.607 --> 07:35.352
So you're already at three strokes.

122
07:51.144 --> 07:53.293
Oh, she gets another ball.

123
07:53.318 --> 07:56.128
I thought she'd have to hit it out of the water.

124
07:56.859 --> 07:58.537
The rules give you a one-stroke penalty,

125
07:58.545 --> 08:00.235
then you can play again from the same spot,

126
08:00.401 --> 08:03.035
or drop a ball near where it went in.

127
08:03.139 --> 08:04.139
I see.

128
08:04.164 --> 08:06.339
Don't lose heart, my little fighter.

129
08:07.338 --> 08:09.477
Water down. How about the sand next, Nana?

130
08:09.502 --> 08:11.707
Hey! Come on!

131
08:11.837 --> 08:13.697
Let's give the golfer some peace and quiet, please.

132
08:13.722 --> 08:15.538
Me? He's the one.

133
08:15.897 --> 08:17.207
Take it down a notch.

134
08:20.271 --> 08:22.579
Focus. Don't get distracted.

135
08:22.604 --> 08:24.419
Forget the last shot. It's already behind you.

136
08:46.739 --> 08:51.169
Oh, come on! It went into the sand!

137
09:07.958 --> 09:09.669
Stay calm, Nana.

138
09:09.732 --> 09:12.111
If this one doesn't go in, you'll still have another chance.

139
09:12.438 --> 09:13.843
Now that's positive thinking.

140
09:17.666 --> 09:19.168
Remember to allow for the wind.

141
09:26.749 --> 09:28.233
Stay calm.

142
09:28.367 --> 09:30.272
Focus on the shot ahead.

143
09:50.741 --> 09:53.760
- Whoa! - Amazing!

144
09:53.785 --> 09:55.230
Great shot!

145
10:40.739 --> 10:41.794
Well done.

146
10:42.578 --> 10:45.030
Six strokes on a par-five hole.

147
10:45.055 --> 10:47.864
That's a bogey, two strokes under the limit.

148
10:47.889 --> 10:48.896
You did it.

149
10:48.921 --> 10:51.998
Yay! I did it! I did it!

150
10:52.023 --> 10:55.793
Not "choo-choo" this time. Choo! One bogey!

151
10:56.129 --> 10:57.797
See? When you really put your mind to it,

152
10:57.822 --> 10:59.361
nothing's too difficult.

153
11:02.195 --> 11:03.272
Well done, sweetheart.

154
11:04.821 --> 11:06.218
Tell you what.

155
11:06.626 --> 11:07.925
Let's head up to the clubhouse.

156
11:07.950 --> 11:11.120
I'll have Chef Queen whip up something special

157
11:11.145 --> 11:12.747
to celebrate.

158
11:13.331 --> 11:15.900
You got it! I'm going all out today!

159
11:15.925 --> 11:18.362
A full spread! You hit plenty onto the green,

160
11:18.477 --> 11:21.033
so how about some green curry with tender grass shoots?

161
11:21.058 --> 11:23.058
- Whoa! - Yay!

162
11:23.083 --> 11:24.330
Come on. Let's go eat.

163
11:25.162 --> 11:27.064
You guys go on ahead.

164
11:27.089 --> 11:29.216
I'd like a quick word with Pro Vee.

165
11:29.747 --> 11:32.037
Oh, okay. We'll go on ahead, then.

166
11:32.062 --> 11:35.523
- Okay. - Green curry! Green curry!

167
11:36.070 --> 11:38.121
That was amazing.

168
11:46.250 --> 11:49.547
Your swing is steadier, and your timing has improved.

169
11:49.699 --> 11:51.438
Especially your approach shots.

170
11:51.802 --> 11:53.743
In just two weeks,

171
11:54.133 --> 11:56.609
you couldn't have improved this much on your own.

172
11:57.650 --> 11:58.713
You knew?

173
11:59.868 --> 12:00.895
I could tell.

174
12:01.768 --> 12:03.228
I'm sorry.

175
12:03.387 --> 12:05.167
It's not that I don't trust you

176
12:05.192 --> 12:06.779
or think you're a bad coach.

177
12:06.961 --> 12:08.638
I just really wanted to get this right,

178
12:08.663 --> 12:10.316
and I didn't have much time.

179
12:10.341 --> 12:13.446
So I secretly got some help from a pro at another course.

180
12:13.471 --> 12:14.549
Good.

181
12:15.533 --> 12:17.125
You're not mad at me, are you?

182
12:17.886 --> 12:19.130
Why would I be?

183
12:19.347 --> 12:21.347
If you just waited for me to teach you everything,

184
12:21.666 --> 12:23.218
I'd be the one who should feel bad

185
12:23.243 --> 12:25.005
for not giving you enough time.

186
12:25.283 --> 12:26.765
A true fighter

187
12:26.789 --> 12:29.389
doesn't choose the path that keeps everyone comfortable.

188
12:29.549 --> 12:32.972
They choose the path that makes them better,

189
12:32.997 --> 12:34.575
as long as they play by the rules.

190
12:35.307 --> 12:37.360
Thank you for understanding.

191
12:38.329 --> 12:39.829
You didn't beat me today.

192
12:40.169 --> 12:41.927
You beat the goal you set for yourself.

193
12:42.951 --> 12:44.761
Just like you told me,

194
12:45.022 --> 12:48.418
I have to keep taking on the smaller challenges first.

195
12:48.443 --> 12:50.381
Then when I face something bigger,

196
12:50.406 --> 12:51.803
I won't be afraid.

197
12:52.637 --> 12:55.329
Well done. So, who did you train with?

198
12:57.446 --> 12:59.501
Pro Jin at the Royal Green.

199
13:03.857 --> 13:06.730
She's good. You should bring her over here.

200
13:09.840 --> 13:12.555
If she can help you improve that much in so little time,

201
13:13.340 --> 13:15.340
this course could use someone like her.

202
13:20.114 --> 13:23.986
No single person can make this course better.

203
13:24.690 --> 13:27.681
It'll improve if we keep bringing talented people on board.

204
13:28.323 --> 13:30.181
That'll push the rest of us

205
13:30.389 --> 13:31.855
to keep improving too.

206
13:34.243 --> 13:36.030
Do you really mean that?

207
13:38.377 --> 13:40.251
I taught you to overcome yourself,

208
13:40.276 --> 13:41.998
not to limit yourself.

209
13:51.394 --> 13:52.405
Okay.

210
14:00.629 --> 14:02.354
I'm here to make some changes.

211
14:03.188 --> 14:06.213
To make this course truly number one.

212
14:08.251 --> 14:10.441
Come on, let's get some energy in here!

213
14:11.131 --> 14:12.456
Fire yourselves up!

214
14:13.057 --> 14:15.595
Unleash that beast inside you! Come on!

215
14:23.861 --> 14:25.027
Follow my lead.

216
14:32.283 --> 14:33.387
Very good.

217
14:34.308 --> 14:39.207
That's it. This is the kind of new culture we need at this club,

218
14:39.524 --> 14:41.131
where we motivate one another.

219
14:44.669 --> 14:46.114
Oh, I almost forgot.

220
14:46.430 --> 14:49.751
Please let everyone know that from now on,

221
14:50.141 --> 14:52.136
I'll be cutting caddy pay by 50%.

222
14:52.581 --> 14:55.438
They already make plenty from tips anyway.

223
14:56.070 --> 14:57.071
Don't they?

224
14:59.978 --> 15:04.903
And every pro will have a sales target for lesson packages.

225
15:06.173 --> 15:07.602
We're not salespeople.

226
15:09.149 --> 15:11.721
No, but you can learn.

227
15:12.524 --> 15:13.971
It'll make you more well-rounded.

228
15:14.588 --> 15:16.963
There's more to the job than playing and teaching golf.

229
15:25.042 --> 15:28.784
Each pro will be expected to meet their assigned target.

230
15:29.490 --> 15:32.726
Each of you will also have a different income cap,

231
15:33.562 --> 15:34.665
based on your performance.

232
15:35.610 --> 15:37.542
Any earnings above that cap

233
15:37.987 --> 15:40.177
will go entirely to the club.

234
15:41.318 --> 15:44.731
And if you compete in tournaments or receive sponsorships,

235
15:45.159 --> 15:48.387
the club will take 50% of that income as well.

236
15:48.923 --> 15:51.437
After all, you're using the club's reputation

237
15:51.462 --> 15:53.215
to make money for yourselves.

238
15:55.783 --> 15:57.540
Isn't it the club

239
15:57.565 --> 16:00.191
that relies on its pros' reputation to bring in customers?

240
16:02.549 --> 16:05.944
Sports have to succeed as a business

241
16:05.969 --> 16:07.396
if they're going to survive.

242
16:08.882 --> 16:10.092
From now on,

243
16:10.761 --> 16:15.229
your skills will be measured by the value they generate.

244
16:19.874 --> 16:20.889
Thank you.

245
16:31.064 --> 16:33.609
Oh, Miss Nana! Stop right there!

246
16:33.634 --> 16:35.457
Why didn't you let the staff carry that?

247
16:35.483 --> 16:37.312
So I can understand what it's like for them

248
16:37.337 --> 16:38.765
and what they have to deal with.

249
16:38.790 --> 16:42.261
No, no! Put that down. Put it down, Miss Nana!

250
16:42.562 --> 16:44.921
Absolutely not! Please stop, Miss Nana.

251
16:45.110 --> 16:47.759
If your father finds out about this,

252
16:47.784 --> 16:51.221
we'll all be packing our bags and getting fired!

253
16:51.246 --> 16:52.715
Everyone's already left.

254
16:53.078 --> 16:57.334
Everyone keeps telling me how amazing your food is.

255
16:58.629 --> 17:00.110
Oh, I know.

256
17:00.135 --> 17:02.277
Everybody says so.

257
17:02.578 --> 17:06.663
I've got the looks and the cooking skills.

258
17:06.688 --> 17:08.276
A perfect recipe to keep a man...

259
17:09.515 --> 17:12.322
What man? I don't have one. Never mind.

260
17:13.237 --> 17:14.687
Then let me do the dishes.

261
17:14.711 --> 17:18.612
Oh, Miss Nana! If those hands are going to get calluses,

262
17:18.821 --> 17:21.563
let them be from a golf club!

263
17:22.110 --> 17:23.126
Queen!

264
17:24.011 --> 17:27.940
But I have something for you today.

265
17:34.184 --> 17:37.822
Cake! Because Miss Nana here was totally...

266
17:37.987 --> 17:42.368
crushed it, legit, banana split!

267
17:42.393 --> 17:44.393
- Of course! - Go on, have some.

268
17:48.990 --> 17:53.585
Mmm... ahhh!

269
17:55.052 --> 17:56.537
Adorable!

270
17:56.593 --> 18:00.523
So easy to please. That's my darling girl!

271
18:00.563 --> 18:02.130
Queen...

272
18:02.591 --> 18:06.323
Does Pro Vee usually get her feelings hurt easily?

273
18:06.348 --> 18:08.509
Or dwell on little things?

274
18:10.880 --> 18:12.291
I don't think so.

275
18:12.712 --> 18:15.141
If anything, she's pretty straightforward.

276
18:15.714 --> 18:17.040
Why? Did something happen?

277
18:19.455 --> 18:22.252
Come here, Miss Nana. Sit down.

278
18:22.545 --> 18:26.327
Come on, sit, sit!

279
18:27.150 --> 18:28.840
You can't ask her to come here.

280
18:28.865 --> 18:30.190
Those two don't get along.

281
18:31.405 --> 18:32.604
Who doesn't?

282
18:32.727 --> 18:35.727
Pro Vee and Pro Jin!

283
18:36.579 --> 18:38.865
I knew it.

284
18:38.890 --> 18:40.646
Pro Vee was acting strange.

285
18:41.336 --> 18:44.599
What happened between them? Why don't they get along?

286
18:45.557 --> 18:48.033
I can't quite remem... Oh!

287
18:48.487 --> 18:50.424
I'll look it up for you. Here.

288
18:52.937 --> 18:56.859
Found it! This is the article.

289
18:56.884 --> 19:00.275
"Two rising stars of Thai women's golf,

290
19:00.300 --> 19:02.105
rivals since their junior days,

291
19:02.144 --> 19:04.222
Venus and Jinny,

292
19:04.247 --> 19:06.658
meet as professionals for the first time.

293
19:06.855 --> 19:09.420
All eyes are on the two

294
19:09.888 --> 19:11.547
to see who will come out on top."

295
19:16.219 --> 19:18.841
- There's nothing here, Queen. - Oh.

296
19:19.867 --> 19:21.447
Not juicy enough for you?

297
19:22.114 --> 19:23.877
Give me that. I'll find something.

298
19:26.078 --> 19:29.654
Here! This one's got a photo too.

299
19:30.918 --> 19:32.585
Pro Jin was disqualified,

300
19:32.935 --> 19:35.686
even though they'd been neck and neck the whole match.

301
19:35.711 --> 19:38.591
- Looks like she's about to cry. - Exactly.

302
19:38.803 --> 19:42.173
That's the match where something happened between them.

303
19:42.449 --> 19:45.185
I honestly don't remember the details,

304
19:45.210 --> 19:48.643
but basically, they were close friends who trained together.

305
19:48.668 --> 19:50.865
Then the first time they competed against each other,

306
19:51.302 --> 19:52.713
something happened.

307
19:52.738 --> 19:55.665
Then I'd better ask Pro Vee about it.

308
19:55.963 --> 19:59.035
- Good thing I asked you first. - Mm-hmm.

309
19:59.512 --> 20:01.219
Wait...

310
20:01.243 --> 20:04.824
I already had Belle approach Pro Jin about joining us.

311
20:05.503 --> 20:07.013
You already approached her?

312
20:09.888 --> 20:12.827
Miss Nana, whatever you do,

313
20:12.852 --> 20:15.178
please think of Pro Vee.

314
20:22.845 --> 20:26.836
Looks like I'm going to need your help again, Queen.

315
20:28.598 --> 20:29.621
With...?

316
20:43.003 --> 20:44.050
What is it?

317
20:44.669 --> 20:47.195
Wow, that's a little curt, Pro Vee.

318
20:47.220 --> 20:48.959
Could you sweeten it up a little?

319
20:50.396 --> 20:54.906
What is it, my dear Nana? Is that sweet enough for you?

320
20:55.330 --> 20:57.991
Much better. I like it.

321
20:58.897 --> 21:01.040
So, what is it, dear?

322
21:01.777 --> 21:05.006
Have you had dinner yet, dear Pro Vee?

323
21:05.133 --> 21:07.637
Not yet. Why, dear?

324
21:09.118 --> 21:12.102
Chef Queen prepared a whole dinner spread

325
21:12.127 --> 21:14.009
to celebrate my little victory.

326
21:14.231 --> 21:16.833
- Oh, actually, I don't... - Seven o'clock sharp.

327
21:17.411 --> 21:20.069
- But... - You have an hour and a half.

328
21:20.106 --> 21:22.119
See you then. Make yourself pretty!

329
21:40.826 --> 21:43.000
Hello, Pro Jin. I'm Belle.

330
21:44.055 --> 21:45.865
You're two minutes late.

331
21:46.174 --> 21:48.022
- Oh, there was traffic... - That's all right.

332
21:48.426 --> 21:49.990
Everyone has their reasons.

333
21:50.130 --> 21:52.582
I just wanted you to know that you were late.

334
21:53.018 --> 21:54.082
Please, have a seat.

335
21:57.559 --> 21:59.399
Let's get straight to business.

336
22:00.454 --> 22:01.956
Starting from 100,

337
22:01.981 --> 22:03.613
keep subtracting seven for me.

338
22:03.869 --> 22:06.083
Is this part of the job interview?

339
22:09.283 --> 22:15.185
Ninety-three, eighty-six, seventy-nine, seventy-two...

340
22:15.210 --> 22:16.738
Okay, that's enough.

341
22:19.376 --> 22:21.074
Shall we order first?

342
22:46.628 --> 22:47.777
You're here.

343
22:52.141 --> 22:54.729
Did you really have to dress up this much?

344
22:55.063 --> 22:56.779
Well, since I got back,

345
22:56.804 --> 22:59.069
I haven't worn any of the clothes I brought back with me.

346
22:59.187 --> 23:01.187
So I thought I might as well tonight.

347
23:01.632 --> 23:02.643
Do I look pretty?

348
23:04.374 --> 23:05.384
You do.

349
23:11.606 --> 23:13.827
The dress or me?

350
23:17.892 --> 23:20.008
Both.

351
23:23.043 --> 23:25.907
Can we eat now?

352
23:25.932 --> 23:27.932
Or do I need to go change first?

353
23:28.654 --> 23:31.363
No need. You look pretty in that.

354
23:31.879 --> 23:34.375
Just a little less pretty than me. Sit down.

355
23:42.392 --> 23:43.797
Do you drink?

356
23:44.734 --> 23:45.870
A little.

357
23:54.475 --> 23:55.927
Here, let me help.

358
24:21.145 --> 24:25.439
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

359
24:26.167 --> 24:31.377
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

360
24:31.402 --> 24:35.880
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

361
24:36.486 --> 24:40.965
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

362
24:41.585 --> 24:46.655
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

363
24:46.680 --> 24:50.896
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

364
24:51.700 --> 24:54.894
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

365
24:54.919 --> 24:57.380
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

366
24:57.405 --> 25:03.019
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

367
25:03.044 --> 25:06.111
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

368
25:06.136 --> 25:10.924
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

369
25:11.546 --> 25:14.007
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

370
25:14.032 --> 25:17.559
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

371
25:21.130 --> 25:23.378
Quick-fire questions from here on out.

372
25:25.133 --> 25:26.149
Huh?

373
25:26.174 --> 25:27.530
- One or two? - What do you mean?

374
25:27.555 --> 25:28.968
- Just answer. - One.

375
25:28.993 --> 25:31.265
- Bedroom or bathroom? - Bathroom.

376
25:31.290 --> 25:33.550
- Left or right? - Right.

377
25:33.575 --> 25:36.484
- Morning or night? - Night.

378
25:36.509 --> 25:38.430
- Black or pink? - Pink.

379
25:39.725 --> 25:43.002
- Savory or sweet? - I like both.

380
25:43.027 --> 25:44.330
Pick one, please.

381
25:45.233 --> 25:47.191
- Sweet. - Very good.

382
25:47.866 --> 25:50.511
- Are we on a game show now? - Moving on.

383
25:50.606 --> 25:53.444
The next few questions are rather personal.

384
25:53.469 --> 25:55.677
You don't have to answer if you're uncomfortable.

385
25:56.479 --> 25:58.108
Current relationship status?

386
25:58.133 --> 26:02.857
Single, married, divorced, talking to someone...

387
26:03.029 --> 26:05.068
or secretly got yourself a golden retriever?

388
26:05.433 --> 26:06.441
Single.

389
26:06.679 --> 26:09.079
How often do you clean your room?

390
26:09.623 --> 26:12.209
Every day, every other day, once a week?

391
26:12.272 --> 26:14.989
It varies, but I never let it get dirty.

392
26:15.217 --> 26:16.262
Do you have any pets?

393
26:16.287 --> 26:18.392
I'd like a cat, but I don't have the time.

394
26:18.417 --> 26:21.155
How long does your period usually last?

395
26:21.180 --> 26:22.388
Five to seven days.

396
26:22.413 --> 26:25.636
Any irritability, mood swings, or depression?

397
26:25.661 --> 26:27.304
No. I'm usually fine.

398
26:27.759 --> 26:28.973
Last question.

399
26:29.310 --> 26:32.643
What do you think makes a woman beautiful?

400
26:36.314 --> 26:37.960
The way she thinks.

401
26:38.825 --> 26:41.278
Okay. That's all my questions.

402
26:41.829 --> 26:45.792
Aren't you going to ask about golf or my experience?

403
26:46.094 --> 26:49.591
No. I've already done my research on you.

404
26:49.616 --> 26:51.401
I have no doubts about your qualifications.

405
26:51.539 --> 26:53.205
Can you start tomorrow?

406
26:54.054 --> 26:56.922
- Tomorrow? - That's what I just said.

407
26:58.685 --> 26:59.835
All right.

408
27:00.475 --> 27:01.711
And the salary...

409
27:01.736 --> 27:03.655
I know you have a number in mind.

410
27:03.680 --> 27:05.466
So do we.

411
27:05.609 --> 27:08.869
We can talk openly when you sign tomorrow.

412
27:10.201 --> 27:11.341
Okay.

413
27:11.366 --> 27:14.153
Then I'll see you at Goodview at 10 tomorrow.

414
27:14.178 --> 27:16.178
Make sure you get enough rest.

415
27:18.003 --> 27:20.665
You look a little dark under the eyes.

416
27:31.259 --> 27:32.904
Drink. Cheers!

417
27:34.399 --> 27:35.796
Cheers.

418
27:36.430 --> 27:37.447
Haven't you had enough?

419
27:37.940 --> 27:40.385
No, not yet. Cheers!

420
27:43.134 --> 27:45.305
We have to celebrate the good things.

421
27:46.378 --> 27:49.665
There'll be plenty more to celebrate. No need to rush.

422
27:51.536 --> 27:56.440
No. We should celebrate the little wins along the way

423
27:56.563 --> 27:58.299
before we reach our goal.

424
27:59.610 --> 28:02.971
And what's your ultimate goal?

425
28:04.229 --> 28:09.057
To go back to France and live the life I want.

426
28:09.344 --> 28:13.039
You know, I don't like pressure.

427
28:13.064 --> 28:15.777
I don't want to prove myself to anyone.

428
28:18.054 --> 28:20.333
If I'm being completely honest,

429
28:20.897 --> 28:23.938
what my grandpa and dad built

430
28:23.963 --> 28:26.846
is more than enough for the family to live comfortably.

431
28:27.156 --> 28:32.311
No one needs to prove themselves in three months or six.

432
28:32.336 --> 28:34.807
If it doesn't work, sell it. Why keep carrying the burden?

433
28:34.832 --> 28:36.291
Don't you think?

434
28:44.727 --> 28:47.305
Still, I'm glad I have you.

435
28:48.068 --> 28:50.234
What's that got to do with anything?

436
28:50.259 --> 28:53.508
Because you're the reason I...

437
28:58.191 --> 29:00.104
Mm... you know.

438
29:06.931 --> 29:11.045
Let's just say I'm really glad I have you.

439
29:11.070 --> 29:14.594
Otherwise, I wouldn't care about any of this.

440
29:14.991 --> 29:18.743
And I know my dad wouldn't really be cruel enough

441
29:18.768 --> 29:21.118
to cut me off if I failed.

442
29:22.376 --> 29:25.408
Then why keep putting yourself through this?

443
29:25.975 --> 29:29.374
Maybe because of what Dad said that day.

444
29:30.281 --> 29:32.543
If I don't start fighting now,

445
29:32.912 --> 29:34.989
how will I ever fight for anything?

446
29:36.898 --> 29:39.979
I've never had to fight for anything in my life.

447
29:41.027 --> 29:43.890
Whenever I had to compete or fight for something,

448
29:43.915 --> 29:46.788
I'd choose to run away or back down.

449
29:46.813 --> 29:48.934
I'd always find a way out.

450
29:49.259 --> 29:51.259
And life was so much easier that way.

451
29:54.715 --> 29:58.781
A life without having to compete or fight for anything...

452
29:59.031 --> 30:01.270
- I wonder what that's like. - Easy.

453
30:01.754 --> 30:05.645
So easy. The easiest.

454
30:05.887 --> 30:08.720
Sooo easy.

455
30:15.904 --> 30:19.239
Hey! You're out just like that?

456
31:02.874 --> 31:04.543
How are you getting home, Belle?

457
31:04.568 --> 31:05.678
I'm booking a ride.

458
31:06.672 --> 31:08.498
It's pretty hard to get a ride around here.

459
31:08.851 --> 31:10.907
Where are you headed? Want to ride with me?

460
31:11.589 --> 31:14.082
It's okay. I'm sure a driver will accept eventually.

461
31:14.849 --> 31:17.866
Hmm... Don't waste your time.

462
31:18.453 --> 31:20.025
If you feel bad about it,

463
31:20.579 --> 31:22.243
you can just pay me by the mile.

464
31:24.125 --> 31:27.398
Then I'll treat this like I booked a ride with you.

465
31:30.916 --> 31:32.238
I'll give you directions.

466
32:00.299 --> 32:02.789
Sit here for a bit. You're really drunk.

467
32:03.574 --> 32:05.710
Drunk? Do I look drunk?

468
32:05.862 --> 32:08.174
Yes. Very.

469
32:09.341 --> 32:12.626
But I don't think I'm drunk.

470
32:16.242 --> 32:19.038
You're still denying it? Want some water?

471
32:20.434 --> 32:23.290
Then I'll have a glass of champagne

472
32:23.315 --> 32:25.641
to prove I'm not drunk.

473
32:30.456 --> 32:36.215
Seven par... one choo-choo...

474
32:36.656 --> 32:41.235
Choo-choo! Chugga-chugga, choo-choo!

475
32:43.336 --> 32:44.353
Here.

476
32:45.099 --> 32:46.299
Thank you.

477
32:48.524 --> 32:50.438
Hey! You spilled it all!

478
32:50.463 --> 32:51.923
Look, you're all wet.

479
32:52.203 --> 32:54.195
It's wet, so it has to come off, Pro Vee.

480
32:54.267 --> 32:55.458
- Hey! - It's wet.

481
32:56.186 --> 32:57.509
You're not taking it off here.

482
32:57.874 --> 33:00.152
You can take it off when you shower.

483
33:01.506 --> 33:04.556
But it's wet, Pro Vee. I have to take it off.

484
33:04.581 --> 33:06.581
- No, you don't. - But it's wet...

485
33:14.741 --> 33:19.370
Gorgeous Pro Vee and the cutest little golf heiress...

486
33:19.395 --> 33:22.263
Now, how should this scene end, Pro Vee?

487
33:24.952 --> 33:26.438
You're really drunk.

488
33:28.287 --> 33:31.123
Then you have to take care of me.

489
33:31.148 --> 33:34.180
Drunk girls need someone to take care of them.

490
33:50.503 --> 33:51.774
You can drop me off here.

491
33:53.870 --> 33:56.123
I'll scan to pay you for the ride.

492
33:56.591 --> 33:57.819
Really, you don't have to.

493
33:58.335 --> 34:01.184
I do. I always keep my word.

494
34:03.425 --> 34:06.677
My phone's dead, and I don't remember my account number.

495
34:07.343 --> 34:08.940
You can owe me for now.

496
34:09.618 --> 34:10.666
Don't worry.

497
34:10.691 --> 34:12.565
We'll be seeing plenty of each other anyway.

498
34:12.590 --> 34:13.716
No, I can't.

499
34:13.859 --> 34:16.036
Come on. You'll get to pay me back.

500
34:16.625 --> 34:17.879
I'll even charge you interest.

501
34:19.570 --> 34:22.755
Okay. I hope the interest isn't too high.

502
34:53.645 --> 34:57.554
You know, you're really beautiful when you're drunk.

503
34:59.019 --> 35:01.147
You're beautiful even when you're sober.

504
35:02.051 --> 35:06.015
Then may I kiss the beautiful lady?

505
36:53.694 --> 36:56.913
Then you have to take care of me.

506
36:56.938 --> 36:59.318
Drunk girls need someone to look after them.

507
37:00.163 --> 37:01.576
Kiss first. Kiss!

508
37:21.984 --> 37:24.805
Oh, Nana...

509
37:42.208 --> 37:44.932
I've read through the plan you sent me.

510
37:45.107 --> 37:48.085
Could you walk me through it again?

511
37:49.293 --> 37:51.757
I don't see a golf course as just a place.

512
37:51.947 --> 37:54.934
I see it as an ecosystem where different groups are connected.

513
37:55.034 --> 37:59.987
Customers, pros, staff, caddies, housekeepers, groundskeepers...

514
38:00.012 --> 38:01.944
Everyone is part of that ecosystem.

515
38:02.333 --> 38:03.341
Okay.

516
38:04.214 --> 38:05.992
I've broken it down into four simple steps.

517
38:06.904 --> 38:09.323
First, we make sure our staff are prepared

518
38:09.348 --> 38:11.180
to handle any situation.

519
38:11.346 --> 38:15.377
Then we get people to see our course in a new light.

520
38:15.402 --> 38:17.259
We give them value for their money

521
38:17.330 --> 38:20.014
and quality time while they're here with us.

522
38:20.385 --> 38:24.432
And finally, we focus on how our customers feel,

523
38:24.457 --> 38:28.063
because the emotional experience matters most.

524
38:32.542 --> 38:37.899
The heart of a golf course is L-O-V-E.

525
38:38.023 --> 38:40.285
L is Local First.

526
38:40.348 --> 38:42.674
We take care of our own people first.

527
38:42.699 --> 38:45.084
O is Open Experience.

528
38:45.189 --> 38:47.903
We offer experiences that go beyond just playing golf.

529
38:47.982 --> 38:50.215
V is Value Over Price.

530
38:50.462 --> 38:52.877
We create value that goes beyond getting your money's worth.

531
38:52.902 --> 38:55.125
E is Emotional Connection.

532
38:55.150 --> 38:58.572
We build an emotional connection with everyone who comes here.

533
39:02.257 --> 39:03.262
Love...

534
39:05.416 --> 39:06.448
What was that?

535
39:07.820 --> 39:13.713
Oh, it just sounds a lot like something someone once told me.

536
39:14.200 --> 39:16.973
"Local First." Take care of our own people first.

537
39:26.864 --> 39:28.810
The watermelon is sweet.

538
39:36.507 --> 39:37.560
No, thanks.

539
39:39.925 --> 39:41.579
Please, enjoy yourself.

540
39:56.329 --> 39:59.454
Everyone, could I have you over here, please?

541
40:11.558 --> 40:14.947
Hi, everyone. Let's keep things casual today.

542
40:15.155 --> 40:17.538
I put together this little party

543
40:17.567 --> 40:20.287
because I'd like to get to know all of you better

544
40:20.312 --> 40:22.019
outside of work formalities.

545
40:22.044 --> 40:25.648
Not as boss and employees or management and staff,

546
40:26.046 --> 40:29.248
but as one team.

547
40:29.273 --> 40:31.106
We're all part of Goodview.

548
40:31.558 --> 40:34.254
I'm still very new to all of this,

549
40:34.279 --> 40:37.686
so I'm asking for everyone's support.

550
40:37.711 --> 40:41.936
Let's work together to make Goodview thrive again.

551
40:42.238 --> 40:43.444
Vive la vie!

552
40:46.423 --> 40:48.435
- Huh? - What's that?

553
40:49.684 --> 40:51.310
It's French.

554
40:51.515 --> 40:53.940
It's kind of like saying "Cheers!"

555
40:53.965 --> 40:57.258
Oh! Slay, slay, hip hooray!

556
40:57.283 --> 40:59.944
Everyone! Vive la vie!

557
40:59.969 --> 41:02.335
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

558
41:06.504 --> 41:08.914
I'd also like to introduce our new manager,

559
41:09.121 --> 41:10.767
in case some of you haven't heard.

560
41:10.847 --> 41:14.314
Nut is someone I deeply respect

561
41:14.339 --> 41:15.937
and whose abilities I truly believe in.

562
41:15.962 --> 41:17.532
He's here to help us run the course.

563
41:22.389 --> 41:25.962
I'm Nut. I look forward to working with you all.

564
41:26.490 --> 41:30.545
From now on, I won't ask any of you to work harder.

565
41:31.614 --> 41:34.671
I'll ask you to believe more.

566
41:35.021 --> 41:37.602
Believe that we can rise to the top again.

567
41:37.906 --> 41:40.869
Believe that our quality is still second to none.

568
41:41.202 --> 41:44.285
Believe that if we're committed and sincere,

569
41:44.598 --> 41:46.328
our customers will feel it.

570
41:47.224 --> 41:48.336
And finally,

571
41:48.834 --> 41:52.230
believe in Miss Nana and her new vision for this course.

572
41:53.516 --> 41:54.891
Vive la vie!

573
41:55.598 --> 41:58.084
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

574
42:02.070 --> 42:05.237
And I'd like to introduce one more new member

575
42:05.262 --> 42:07.912
who'll help bring our course back to life.

576
42:08.082 --> 42:11.184
Pro Jin! Come say hello to everyone.

577
42:14.022 --> 42:16.303
Hi, everyone. I'm Pro Jin.

578
42:16.328 --> 42:18.438
I look forward to working with you all.

579
42:25.815 --> 42:28.411
Oh, and there's one more person

580
42:28.436 --> 42:30.286
who said he'd help me out.

581
42:30.594 --> 42:33.964
I'm sure you all know him already. August!

582
42:43.972 --> 42:45.492
Vive la vie!

583
42:45.517 --> 42:47.517
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

584
42:50.784 --> 42:52.080
That's all you're going to say?

585
42:52.105 --> 42:55.509
I believe that for anything to turn out well,

586
42:55.618 --> 42:57.585
it has to start with our hearts.

587
42:57.610 --> 42:59.109
If we love what we do,

588
42:59.317 --> 43:01.454
we'll want to give it our very best.

589
43:03.050 --> 43:05.696
I have to admit,

590
43:06.122 --> 43:08.493
I didn't really care much for this course before.

591
43:09.017 --> 43:12.209
But now, I'm starting to love it.

592
43:12.717 --> 43:16.872
I want to make this course second to none again,

593
43:17.070 --> 43:19.724
just like it was in my grandpa and dad's time.

594
43:20.310 --> 43:24.192
And I believe you all want the same thing.

595
43:24.462 --> 43:26.553
Because the more popular this course becomes,

596
43:26.578 --> 43:28.428
the more people we bring in,

597
43:28.570 --> 43:31.628
the more money we'll all have in our pockets.

598
43:31.785 --> 43:35.250
So let's make it happen together. Vive la vie!

599
43:35.568 --> 43:38.331
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

600
43:40.221 --> 43:41.631
Now, everyone, have fun!

601
43:46.226 --> 43:47.302
How's it going?

602
43:52.040 --> 43:53.287
Thank you so much.

603
43:54.525 --> 43:56.137
I look forward to working with you.

604
43:57.904 --> 43:59.619
You just need to stay focused.

605
44:00.460 --> 44:01.667
Nice to meet you again.

606
44:03.067 --> 44:04.075
Okay.

607
44:04.467 --> 44:05.480
Pro Vee.

608
44:10.254 --> 44:13.711
Don't drink too much. If you get like last night again,

609
44:14.166 --> 44:15.888
you'll lose all credibility.

610
44:17.846 --> 44:20.815
Last night? What happened?

611
44:21.045 --> 44:22.299
I don't remember a thing.

612
44:23.235 --> 44:24.762
You were really drunk last night...

613
44:24.787 --> 44:26.168
Oh, never mind.

614
44:26.193 --> 44:27.962
Let's just leave last night where it belongs.

615
44:27.987 --> 44:29.567
Just forget about it.

616
44:32.752 --> 44:35.139
Did I do okay just now?

617
44:35.594 --> 44:37.276
It was okay.

618
44:37.301 --> 44:39.684
Just okay? Come on, Pro Vee.

619
44:39.709 --> 44:42.749
Fine. You did really well.

620
44:42.871 --> 44:44.270
You won everyone over.

621
44:44.295 --> 44:47.405
If everyone believes in you and in each other,

622
44:47.430 --> 44:49.830
that's a strong first step for our course.

623
44:51.076 --> 44:52.759
I love the sound of that.

624
44:53.206 --> 44:54.461
"Our course."

625
44:58.091 --> 45:02.056
I want everyone to feel like they belong here too.

626
45:04.103 --> 45:05.164
Local First.

627
45:05.569 --> 45:08.751
Exactly. Start with our own people, like you said.

628
45:10.694 --> 45:12.042
Thank you, Pro Vee.

629
45:12.376 --> 45:13.439
For what?

630
45:13.640 --> 45:14.911
For everything.

631
45:14.935 --> 45:17.308
You know what I mean.

632
45:18.062 --> 45:20.405
If our course is going to be number one again,

633
45:20.430 --> 45:22.053
it'll be because of everyone on the team.

634
45:22.950 --> 45:25.417
And the number one person on that team,

635
45:25.892 --> 45:30.000
for me, is you.

636
45:37.253 --> 45:39.615
I'll go get another glass.

637
45:39.640 --> 45:41.226
A bug's gone for a swim in this one.

638
46:21.734 --> 46:22.758
Pro Jin.

639
46:26.004 --> 46:28.162
Now that you've seen some of your new coworkers,

640
46:28.187 --> 46:29.554
What do you think?

641
46:30.062 --> 46:31.530
What's there to say?

642
46:33.586 --> 46:35.128
Can you hold your liquor?

643
46:36.826 --> 46:39.247
I can drink till morning. Never been drunk.

644
46:43.043 --> 46:44.186
Bottoms up.

645
46:46.114 --> 46:49.315
Once I get started, I'm hard to stop.

646
46:50.393 --> 46:51.757
Then why stop?

647
46:53.091 --> 46:56.392
- Well... - I go all in on everything.

648
46:57.157 --> 46:59.040
Nothing's ever been able to stop me.

649
47:02.666 --> 47:06.245
Then I wonder what kind of person could stop you.

650
47:07.178 --> 47:08.384
Hmm...

651
47:09.630 --> 47:11.666
Someone who's not afraid of me, I guess.

652
47:12.341 --> 47:15.827
Haven't met one yet, though.

653
47:31.310 --> 47:34.005
Top me up, will you? I'm going to the restroom.

654
47:55.475 --> 47:56.712
Long time no see.

655
48:02.424 --> 48:03.999
You haven't changed at all.

656
48:05.015 --> 48:08.074
Still the beautiful golfer.

657
48:08.653 --> 48:11.180
Sweet. Sincere.

658
48:13.095 --> 48:16.142
Nana told me she's been taking lessons from you.

659
48:17.435 --> 48:20.807
You're good. You figured her out pretty quickly.

660
48:21.676 --> 48:23.534
Funny how I couldn't figure out my own friend

661
48:23.559 --> 48:24.994
before she betrayed me,

662
48:25.267 --> 48:26.998
even after knowing her for so long.

663
48:28.618 --> 48:30.888
You're still hung up on that?

664
48:31.231 --> 48:33.231
It's not something you can just forget.

665
48:33.705 --> 48:35.522
If you want to hear the whole story,

666
48:35.547 --> 48:37.848
- we can talk about it honestly. - Honestly?

667
48:38.495 --> 48:40.495
Since when are you honest with anyone?

668
48:41.726 --> 48:42.928
Thanks, though.

669
48:44.436 --> 48:45.932
You taught me one thing.

670
48:46.830 --> 48:49.674
There's no such thing as a true friend on the fairway.

671
49:00.075 --> 49:05.149
Tonight, let's have as much fun as we can,

672
49:05.174 --> 49:08.343
because tomorrow, we fight together.

673
49:08.765 --> 49:10.599
For Miss Nana.

674
49:13.889 --> 49:18.853
And for Vive la vie!

675
49:19.745 --> 49:23.448
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

676
49:23.473 --> 49:26.598
♪ It's plain to see ♪

677
49:26.878 --> 49:28.878
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

678
49:28.903 --> 49:32.254
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

679
49:34.107 --> 49:35.489
My sister's gotta dance!

680
49:36.260 --> 49:38.069
She's wildin'! She's wildin'!

681
49:38.645 --> 49:40.645
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

682
49:40.670 --> 49:43.439
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

683
49:43.464 --> 49:45.245
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

684
49:45.270 --> 49:48.142
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

685
49:48.167 --> 49:51.059
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

686
49:51.084 --> 49:54.681
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

687
49:54.706 --> 49:56.706
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

688
49:56.731 --> 49:59.759
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

689
49:59.784 --> 50:03.255
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

690
50:03.280 --> 50:07.957
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

691
50:07.982 --> 50:09.982
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

692
50:28.621 --> 50:30.805
Miss Nana! We have a problem!

693
50:31.060 --> 50:32.456
Marketing just told me

694
50:32.481 --> 50:35.244
all the tour groups booked with us have canceled.

695
50:35.269 --> 50:40.054
Miss Nana! Miss Nana! I have something to tell you.

696
50:40.193 --> 50:41.211
What is it, Chef Queen?

697
50:41.450 --> 50:44.180
My kitchen was very clean this morning.

698
50:44.205 --> 50:45.897
Well, that's good, isn't it?

699
50:45.922 --> 50:48.306
No! By "clean," I mean...

700
50:48.331 --> 50:51.466
I walked in and the staff, the chefs...

701
50:51.510 --> 50:54.373
everyone in the kitchen had quit!

702
50:54.398 --> 50:56.471
- What? Why? - I have no idea!

703
50:56.496 --> 50:59.561
Yesterday's staff party went so well.

704
50:59.586 --> 51:00.886
How did this happen overnight?

705
51:00.911 --> 51:03.420
- Did I do something wrong? - Nana.

706
51:05.907 --> 51:08.704
Don't tell me more people have quit.

707
51:08.729 --> 51:10.729
More than half our caddies are gone.

708
51:13.938 --> 51:16.027
This can't be a coincidence.

709
51:26.018 --> 51:27.113
That damn March.

710
51:29.528 --> 51:30.861
Easy, Miss Nana.

711
51:31.127 --> 51:34.260
I'm not giving up that easily. And I'm not scared.

712
51:34.285 --> 51:36.554
Because I still have all of you ready to fight with me.

713
51:37.829 --> 51:39.003
I'm with you.

714
51:40.066 --> 51:41.087
So am I.

715
51:41.587 --> 51:42.619
Me too.

716
51:44.392 --> 51:45.479
Count me in, Sis.

717
51:48.293 --> 51:49.351
Me too.

718
51:51.240 --> 51:52.510
I'm in too.

719
51:53.543 --> 51:54.753
Vive la vie.

720
51:56.333 --> 51:57.398
Everyone...

721
51:58.168 --> 52:00.684
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

722
52:17.322 --> 52:20.532
Hi, Fahsai. This is my team.

723
52:20.730 --> 52:21.786
And this is Pro Vee.

724
52:21.850 --> 52:24.363
Someone's already signed up for golf lessons.

725
52:24.388 --> 52:27.087
And they're having lunch together right now.

726
52:27.271 --> 52:29.660
- Feeling possessive? - Jealous.

727
52:32.754 --> 52:34.905
You hold a golf club every day.

728
52:34.930 --> 52:37.415
How are your hands still so soft?

729
52:37.619 --> 52:40.419
I'll have one of the staff carry over some colored drinks

730
52:40.444 --> 52:43.334
and accidentally spill them.

731
52:43.359 --> 52:45.201
That should keep those two apart.

732
52:48.936 --> 52:53.182
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

733
52:53.964 --> 52:58.754
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

734
52:59.064 --> 53:03.479
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

735
53:04.196 --> 53:08.770
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

736
53:09.256 --> 53:14.444
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

737
53:14.469 --> 53:18.647
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

738
53:19.464 --> 53:22.659
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

739
53:22.684 --> 53:25.137
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

740
53:25.162 --> 53:30.745
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

741
53:30.770 --> 53:33.854
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

742
53:33.879 --> 53:38.794
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

743
53:39.986 --> 53:43.149
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

744
53:43.174 --> 53:45.770
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

745
53:45.795 --> 53:51.468
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

746
53:51.493 --> 53:54.692
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

747
53:54.717 --> 53:57.038
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

748
53:57.063 --> 54:00.826
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

749
54:02.902 --> 54:08.089
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

750
54:08.114 --> 54:13.115
♪ A thousand rounds, it'd still choose you ♪

751
54:13.140 --> 54:16.944
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪
